    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "B737-400\nSafety Instructions\nInstructions de Sécurité\nInstrucciones de Seguridad\nSicherheitsanleitungen\nUSAir",
      "EVACUATION PROCEDURES\nPROCEDIMIENTOS DE EVACUACION\nEVAKUIERUNGSVERFAHREN\nPROCEDURES D'EVACUATION\nA-A\nA-A\nA\nExit Row Seating\n•\nSi usted está sentado en una fila de salida, y no\npuede leer, hablar o entender inglés, sirvase\ncontactar a un representante de USAir o USAir\nExpress para que se le cambie de asiento.\n• Falls Sich Ihr sitz in einer Reihe an einem der\nausgänge befindet, und wenn Sie weder English\nlesen, sprechen oder verstehen können, wenden\nSic sich bitte an einen Vertreter von USAir oder\nUsAIr express, der Innen emen anderen\nSitzplatz suweisen wird.\n• Si vous êtes assis près d'une issue de secours, et\nvous n'êtes pas en mesure de lire l'anglais, ni de le\nparler ou de le comprendre, veuillez contacter un\nrepresentant de la compagne USAIr OU USAI\nExpress pour obtenir un autre siège.\nIf you are seated in an exit row, please review the\n- following. Federal Aviation Regulations require that\npassengers seated in this row meet the selection\ncriteria and are willing and able to operate une exit\nand assist others in the event of an emergency in\nwhich a crewmember is not available to do so.\nPlease identifv the exit nearest to vou and review the\ncorresponding functions found on this \"Safety\nInstructions\" card.\nPlease contact your Flight Attendant for reseating if\nyou have a condition, which is not apparent, that\nwould prevent you from performing the functions\nshown on this \"Safety Instructions\" card; would be\nharmed from doing so; do not wish to do so; or if\nany of the following apply:\n•\nMobility, strength or dexterity in both arms and\nhands, and both legs is not sufficient to perform\nthe functions and assist others, including:\nReaching the exit quickly\nReaching in every direction for mechanisms used\n-Operating the exit\n-Securing the exit open\n-Removing obstructions (maintaining balance\nwhile doing so)\n-Quickly passing through the exit\n• You are less than 15 years old, require assistance\nfrom someone else to nerform one or more of the\nfunctions, or would be prevented from doing so\nbecause of a condition or responsibility, such as\ncaring for a small child.\n• You cannot sufficiently impart information orally\nto others or understand oral crew commands.\n• You cannot read or understand the written and\ngraphic instructions provided or require assistance\n(other than a hearing aid) to hear or understand\ninstructions shouted by a crewmember.\n•You do not have the visual capacity to assess\nconditions outside of the exit or perform any other\nTine on decerined witholt the accictance of vichal\naids other than contact lenses or eyeglasses.\nIn the event of an emergency, follow the directions\nand hand signals of your crew. If a crewmember is\nnot available to assist you, follow the instructions on\nthe \"Safety Instructions\" card and posted signs. Wait\nuntil the airplane has stopped before opening the exit\nand look through the window, assessing conditions\n(looking for smoke, fire or obstructions) to\ndetermine whether it is safe to proceed. If it is safe to\ndo so, operate the exit and assist others according to\nthe instructions. Assess, select and follow a safe path\naway from the airplane.\nYour Flight Attendants will be glad to answer any\nquestions you may have.",
      "BRACE POSITIONS\nPOSICIONES PARA PROTECCION\nNOTLANDUNGEN\nPOSITIONS DE PROTECTION\nRESTRICTIONS\nRESTRICCIONES\nBESCHRÄNKUNGEN\nINTERDICTIONS\nWATER EVACUATION\nEVACUACION EN EL MAR\nEVAKUIERUNG ZU WASSER\nEVACUATION SUR L'EAU\nCopyright©1989 USAir\n737-4-ECPS\nC/C 190-0348\nRev. 12/92\n4/93\n2002.127.605"
    ],
